{"name":"Indiecraft","title":"Indiecraft","revision":236594,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Indiecraft","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Indiecraft is an aesthetic that emerged in the mid-2000s alongside Hipness Purgatory, in which they both share common aspects. It's characterized by its heavy emphasis on handcrafted imagery (ex. collage and maquettes), charming and cozy atmosphere utilizing warm colors, and childlike imagination using techniques like stop motion and 3D illustrations of papercraft-like objects (especially in video games)."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The aesthetic is characterized by handcrafted imagery that places emphasis on childlike imagination. With the use of warm colors, puppets, and collage layouts, Indiecraft creates a cozy, kooky and charming atmosphere. Materials like felt and construction paper are used to make the designs appear handcrafted."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Precursors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pingu (1986)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Julie - Les Colocs (1992)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Neverhood (1996)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Skullmonkeys (1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gregory Horror Show (Anime) (1999-2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Boombots (1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Klaymen Gun-Hockey (1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ride On Shooting Star - The Pillows (2000)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film/Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pecola (Cartoon) (2001-2002)"},{"kind":"list","text":"31 Minutos (2003-2014)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Moral Orel (2005-2008, 2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"PES shorts (2008-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Phoebe in Wonderland (Movie) (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Amazing World of Gumball (Cartoon) (2011-2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Adventures of Abney and Teal (Cartoon) (2011-2012)"},{"kin